{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"c3c1900432cda0a4f69f1ac0741114082bfd3628e078f08e3f24431b5fee9cda","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate protocol and agent-facing documentation","key_entities":["CLAUDE.md","CLAUDE.md:112-121","examples/claude-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md:136","examples/claude-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md:135","examples/claude-skills/rebar-janitor/SKILL.md","docs/","CONTRIBUTING.md","examples/","REVIEW_RESULT","norm_id"],"problem_keywords":["advisory remediation","agent guidance","gate protocol","mandatory remediation","convergence","plan review","compute efficiency"],"propositions":["Mandatory advisory remediation in CLAUDE.md gate protocols (lines 112-121) creates excessive remediation loops (95% of edits mint new findings) and drives 4+-round tail consuming 60% of gate compute.","The MUST-remediate-all-valid-advisories mandate should be replaced with neutral judgment framing ('apply advisories that genuinely improve the plan') while retaining blocking-verdict remediation and sign-every-round requirements.","Two echoes of the mandatory-remediation rule exist in committed skill examples (rebar-implement/SKILL.md:136 and rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md:135) and must be softened to the same judgment framing while preserving their BLOCK-must-remediate instructions.","Rebar-janitor's Remediation Plan phase and rebar-implement's completion-verifier close-gate (line 254) are distinct concepts and must remain unchanged.","After loosening the mandate, advisory uptake rate and rounds-to-pass will be observed via REVIEW_RESULT sidecars (norm_id survival across rounds as proxy for advisory addressal) per epic 9d50 AC2 measurement framework."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785824810003445973,"uuid":"b3f2686a-9e84-4ad8-96c7-c29b8aceefbf"}